# An unnamed schema followed by a named one: both are views (the unnamed one is "main"), side by side.
title "A field beside a network"
schema plane x=[-3,3] y=[-3,3] grid=false axes=false
mark clock param value=0
mark F field vx={-y} vy={x} style=lines
mark p dot x={2*cos(clock)} y={2*sin(clock)} trail=1.5s label="planet"
schema net graph label="a tiny net"
mark x1 box input label="x₁"
mark h1 box output label="h"
link w1 arrow x1 -> h1 label="w₁"
Say: "A planet circles in its |go|field, and a network sits beside it."
@go morph clock.value 0 -> 3.14 2s ease=linear
